{"prototypeToken":{"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":true}},"height":1,"width":1,"name":"Mercurial Knight","actorLink":false,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/tokens/mercurial-knight.webp","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"negative":false,"priority":0},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/subjects/mercurial-knight.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":1},"name":"Mercurial Knight","type":"npc","effects":[],"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":45,"temp":0,"max":45,"details":""},"ac":{"value":21,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":20,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":[],"details":""},"level":{"value":3},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Mercurial knights are adaptable constructs that can change between solid and liquid forms. According to legend, an ancient artificer, on a quest to create the perfect bodyguard, constructed the first mercurial knight out of pure quicksilver. Unable, or perhaps unwilling, to choose between a bulky knight and an agile fighter, the crafter attempted to make a guard capable of both, able to shift on a whim to better protect against possible intruders. Whether this invention was a stroke of genius or a sign of mercury-induced foolishness usually depends on which end of the knight's sword you find yourself on.</p>\n<p>At first glance, a mercurial knight appears as a standard suit of armor, though slight ripples across its form hint at its true nature. Composed almost entirely of quicksilver, mercurial knights can will themselves to solidify, becoming imposing and stalwart defenders. In liquid form, a knight loses some protection but gains the speed and grace to make it a deadly combatant, and its liquid body is able to fit through the smallest crack. This allows for quick movement throughout the battlefield, either to confront intruders or to make a rapid escape.</p>\n<p>In battle, a mercurial knight often confronts an intruder while in its solid form, using strong armor to deflect blows and soak up damage. When the time is right, it liquefies, providing the construct with a lithe form and powerful attacks to force the intruders back. Any party facing such a creation must approach with caution and employ smart tactics or risk being outmaneuvered by the perfect bodyguard.</p>\n<h2>Volatile Allegiance</h2>\n<p>Mercurial knights may change who they consider to be allies on a whim. These decisions are sometimes based on who is winning, but other times they are inscrutable. As a result, they often end up stationed far from their masters during a fight.</p>\n<h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 7/18/30 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, slashing), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Stealth)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, dexterity, energy resistant (negative, positive), poison, strength, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Strange and Unusual","authors":"Matt Cavanaugh","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":4},"dex":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":0},"wis":{"mod":1},"cha":{"mod":1}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":9,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":12,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":9,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":6,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":9},"athletics":{"base":9},"stealth":{"base":7}},"traits":{"value":["construct"],"rarity":"common","size":{"value":"med"}}},"img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/Portraits/mercurial-knight.webp","items":[{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","name":"Darkvision","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Darkvision]</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"darkvision","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Bestiary","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"interaction","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""},"weapon":{"value":""}},"type":"action","flags":{"core":{}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688926454878,"modifiedTime":1688926454878,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.qCCLZhnp2HhP3Ex6","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"_id":"kzOFfxc9i7cFFQ0y"},{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Mercurial Form","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The knight flows from solid to liquid throughout combat, gaining and losing effects based on the form it occupies; in addition to its Reform reaction, it can change its form as a single action. The knight defaults to its solid form, and where its statistics differ, the listed statistics apply for its solid form unless stated otherwise. While in its liquid form, the knight is able to move through any opening large enough for water. The knight also has a different Strike depending on its form, a mercury hammer in solid form and a mercury sword in liquid form.</p>"},"rules":[{"key":"RollOption","option":"mercurial-form","suboptions":[{"label":"Solid","value":"solid"},{"label":"Liquid","value":"liquid"}],"toggleable":true,"value":true,"alwaysActive":true,"selection":"solid"},{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":"land-speed","value":10,"predicate":["mercurial-form:liquid"]},{"category":"simple","damage":{"base":{"damageType":"bludgeoning","dice":1,"die":"d6","modifier":6}},"attackModifier":12,"key":"Strike","label":"Mercury Hammer","predicate":["mercurial-form:solid"]},{"category":"simple","damage":{"base":{"damageType":"slashing","dice":1,"die":"d12","modifier":8}},"attackModifier":12,"key":"Strike","label":"Mercury Sword","predicate":["mercurial-form:liquid"]},{"key":"Weakness","type":"bludgeoning","value":5,"predicate":["mercurial-form:solid"]},{"key":"Resistance","type":["piercing","slashing"],"value":5,"predicate":["mercurial-form:solid"]},{"key":"Resistance","type":"bludgeoning","value":5,"predicate":["mercurial-form:liquid"]},{"key":"Weakness","type":["piercing","slashing"],"value":5,"predicate":["mercurial-form:liquid"]},{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":"ac","value":-4,"predicate":["mercurial-form:liquid"]},{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":["fortitude"],"value":-3,"predicate":["mercurial-form:liquid"]},{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":"reflex","value":3,"predicate":["mercurial-form:liquid"]}],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"interaction","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"effects":[],"_id":"u8DgvMSzGaPdmlfc","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.3.0","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688926484950,"modifiedTime":1691130200070,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Reform","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The Mercurial Knight would take physical damage that it is weak to</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The knight changes to a liquid or solid form, whichever is not its current form. Apply the triggering damage after the change.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"category":"defensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"effects":[],"_id":"iR1QMkFLuBMedFvv","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688927755698,"modifiedTime":1688927777908,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Mercury Splash","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The Mercurial Knight is in its liquid form</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The knight sprays raw mercury from its body in a @Template[type:cone|distance:15]. All creatures within this cone take @Damage[2d6[bludgeoning],1d4[poison]]{2d6 bludgeoning damage and 1d4 poison} damage, with a @Check[type:reflex|dc:17|basic:true] save.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"action"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":2},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"effects":[],"_id":"XUx4EmdxdhaXpuDS","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.3.0","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688927795323,"modifiedTime":1691261013110,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}}],"flags":{"core":{}},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"6.1.0","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1685401626117,"modifiedTime":1736542895305,"lastModifiedBy":"l2rbNx2a8f5ocpeL","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"_id":"LWSvM2THzmycayqx","folder":"rnSyamM9GQTIpuOo","ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"sort":1100000}